Stop writing junk body and malformed DOI links on migrated publications.

Two mappings in the biblio publication migration produce bad data on every
affected node.

body/value was mapped from {biblio}.biblio_full_text. That column is a flag
recording whether full text exists, not the text itself, and it holds 0 for
every row -- so all 8169 migrated publications ended up with a body of the
literal string "0", rendered under a "Full Text" label. Biblio has no
body-equivalent column, so the mapping is removed rather than repointed.

field_pub_doi/uri concatenated a constant https://dx.doi.org/ base with
biblio_doi without inspecting it, but that column is dirty. On agsci's 8173
rows: 4382 are empty or whitespace-only, ~80 already hold a full
https://doi.org/ URL, and 14 carry stray padding. The result was a link to a
bare https://dx.doi.org/ on the empty ones, and doubled-up URLs such as
"https://dx.doi.org/     https://doi.org/10.1371/..." on the rest.

Trim first, so whitespace-only values register as empty for skip_on_empty
(which uses empty() and would otherwise let "   " through); skip the property
rather than the row when no DOI is present; then normalise with a regex that
strips any existing doi.org prefix before applying the canonical one.

--- a/modules/osu_migrate_content/migrations/upgrade_d7_biblio_publication.yml
+++ b/modules/osu_migrate_content/migrations/upgrade_d7_biblio_publication.yml
@@ -39,22 +39,39 @@
       source: author
       process:
         value: name
-  body/value: biblio_full_text
-  body/format:
-    - plugin: default_value
-      default_value: 'full_html'
+  # NOTE: {biblio}.biblio_full_text is a flag recording whether full text
+  # exists, not the text itself -- every row holds 0. Mapping it to the body
+  # stamped the string "0" onto every migrated publication. Biblio has no
+  # body-equivalent column, so body is intentionally left unmapped.
   field_pub_abstract/value: biblio_abst_e
   field_pub_abstract/format:
     - plugin: default_value
       default_value: 'full_html'
   field_pub_issn: biblio_issn
-  field_pub_doi/title: biblio_doi
+  # biblio_doi is dirty: about half the rows are empty or whitespace, ~80
+  # already contain a full https://doi.org/ URL, and a few carry stray
+  # padding. Blindly concatenating the base URL gave a bare
+  # https://dx.doi.org/ on the empty ones and a double-prefixed URL on the
+  # rest. Trim first so whitespace-only counts as empty for skip_on_empty
+  # (which uses empty() and would otherwise pass "   " through), skip the
+  # property when there is no DOI, then normalise: the regex strips any
+  # existing doi.org prefix before applying the canonical one.
+  field_pub_doi/title:
+    - plugin: callback
+      callable: trim
+      source: biblio_doi
+    - plugin: skip_on_empty
+      method: process
   field_pub_doi/uri:
-    - plugin: concat
-      source:
-        - constants/doi_base_url
-        - biblio_doi
-      delimiter: ''
+    - plugin: callback
+      callable: trim
+      source: biblio_doi
+    - plugin: skip_on_empty
+      method: process
+    - plugin: str_replace
+      regex: true
+      search: '~^(?:https?://(?:dx\.)?doi\.org/)?(.+)$~i'
+      replace: 'https://dx.doi.org/$1'
   field_pub_year_publication: biblio_year
   field_pub_date_published/value:
     - plugin: normalize_biblio_date
